        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "D. Employees in all Selling classifications may dispute any return after receiving the record of compensation listing that return. Once a return is disputed, the Employer shall have sixty (60) days to provide documentation that the return has been properly charged back. If the return is not substantiated within this sixty (60) day period, the Employer shall credit the salesperson for any lost commission on the next payday following the expiration of the sixty (60) day period. However, if the Employer is able to substantiate the charge back within the next sixty (60) days, the commission will be deducted from the salesperson's paycheck.",
            "block_bbox": [
                347,
                287,
                1482,
                490
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
